This package is a standalone rewrite of dsh-playwright-browser by Clizo1209,
used under the MIT License. The original project lives at:

    https://github.com/Clizo1209/dsh-playwright-browser

Upstream ships TypeScript sources, so this is a port rather than a repackage:
the target parser and the browser controller follow its design closely, while
the plugin surface is rebuilt for this repository's conventions. The
differences are deliberate:

  - Skill gating. Upstream registers ten browser_* tools globally, so every
    agent under every preset carries them. Here they mount into an agent only
    once it loads the `browser` skill, matching tool-file-canvas and the vision
    toolkit. This repository owns no agent preset, and a skill gate is how a
    profile-level plugin grants tools without one.

  - playwright-core instead of playwright. The `playwright` package downloads
    Chromium, Firefox, and WebKit in a postinstall step; playwright-core
    downloads nothing. The launch fallback (Playwright Chromium, then system
    Chrome, then Edge) already covers finding a browser.

  - Screenshots resolve against the session workspace rather than the harness
    process cwd, and are declared as artifacts. That puts them inside the
    artifact canvas's roots, so `show_file` can render one for the user.

  - Two added guards: navigation to cloud instance-metadata addresses is
    refused, and `userDataDir` may not point at a real browser profile.

  - The hand-rolled parameter/type machinery is dropped in favour of
    `defineTool` from @deepseek-ai/dsh-tools, which infers the same types.

